FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      decomposeParDict;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

numberOfSubdomains 192;
method          scotch;

// THIS IS THE MESH-STAGE DECOMPOSITION: 192 ranks, scotch.
//
// WHY IT IS PART OF THE MESH RECIPE. snappyHexMesh runs in parallel on this
// decomposition, and parallel snappyHexMesh is decomposition-dependent: a
// different rank count or a different method builds a different mesh. So the
// method and the count are fixed here, with the rest of the mesh recipe, and
// hpc/mesh_hpc12.pbs reads the count from this file and refuses an allocation
// with fewer slots.
//
// WHAT RAN. All six wake-refined Condition CR meshes on HPC12 (scratch
// argus/mesh/SWB_r2, SWC_r2, SWF_r2, SWH_r2, SWM_r2 and SWW_r2) carry exactly
// this pair, and every one of their snappyHexMesh logs reports nProcs 192.
//
// THE SOLVE CASE IS DECOMPOSED DIFFERENTLY, ON PURPOSE. hpc/stage_solve_case.sh
// builds the solve case from this recipe plus the finished mesh and rewrites
// its decomposition to 128 ranks by default, hierarchical 8 by 2 by 8. All
// six r2 solves ran 128 ranks, hierarchical; the 8 by 2 by 8 split matches the
// 128-rank case definitions. 128 is four 32-core typej nodes on fpt-medium.
// Re-decomposing a finished mesh does not change the mesh. Do not solve with
// this file unchanged: solve_hpc12.pbs reads the rank count from the case and
// would decompose the solve onto 192.
//
// WHAT THE METHOD COSTS, MEASURED on the ARGUS baseline at 4 levels below
// production, scotch against hierarchical from the same inputs:
//     wing wetted area   scotch 1.28019 m2   hierarchical 1.28026 m2   0.005%
//     total cells        243,379             241,911                   0.60%
// Small, but not zero, which is why the method is a mesh setting and not a
// scheduling one. Changing it changes the mesh.
//
// WHERE SCOTCH IS MISSING. DelftBlue's openfoam-org/12 module was built
// without it (only the dummy libscotchDecomp stub), and decomposePar there
// dies with "you are trying to use scotch but do not have the scotch library
// loaded". The HPC12 OpenFOAM-12 build meshed all six r2 cases with it, and
// the Ubuntu OpenFOAM-12 package has it too. Meshing on a machine without it
// means editing this file, which is a mesh change: record it.
//
// TWO THINGS THIS FILE MUST NOT CONTAIN, both learned by being bitten:
//   1. The subdomain-count keyword followed by a space, anywhere else including
//      comments. Older job scripts rewrite every line carrying it, comments
//      too. That altered this file mid-job, and the recipe gate then correctly
//      refused the case on resubmit for not matching its own manifest.
//   2. A close-comment token. One appeared inside a quoted sed example in an
//      earlier version of this file and OpenFOAM stopped at "found on line 37
//      the punctuation token".
